Bug 1: `weekYear` only handles the case where week === 1 and month === 11 (December). It doesn't handle the case where the date is in early January and belongs to the previous week-year.

For en-gb: yearStart = 4. So week 1 of 2021 starts on Jan 4, 2021 (the first week containing Jan 4). Jan 1-3, 2021 are in the last week of 2020 → week() returns... let's see: `week()` for 2021-01-01 with yearStart=4: month() = 0, not 11. yearStartDay = 2021-01-04. yearStartWeek = 2021-01-04 startOf week (Monday, weekStart=1 for en-gb) = 2021-01-04, minus 1ms = 2021-01-03T23:59:59.999. diffInWeek = this.diff(yearStartWeek, 'week', true) → negative for Jan 1 → returns `d(this).startOf('week').week()`. startOf('week') for Jan 1, 2021 (Friday) with weekStart=1 → Monday Dec 28, 2020. Then `.week()` on Dec 28, 2020: month()=11, date()=28 > 25 → nextYearStartDay = 2021-01-04; thisEndOfWeek = endOf week of Dec 28, 2020 = Sunday Jan 3, 2021 23:59:59.999. Is 2021-01-04 before 2021-01-03T23:59:59.999? No. So skip. yearStartDay = 2020-01-04 (startOf year 2020 = 2020-01-01, .date(4) → 2020-01-04). yearStartWeek = 2020-01-04 startOf week = 2020-01-06 (Monday) minus 1ms = 2020-01-05T23:59:59.999. diffInWeek = Dec 28, 2020 - Jan 5, 2020 in weeks = 358 days/7 ≈ 51.14 → ceil = 52. So week() = 52.

So for 2021-01-01: week() = 52, month() = 0, year() = 2021. weekYear() → not (week===1 && month===11) → returns 2021. But expected 2020.

The fix (upstream): 

```js
export default (o, c) => {
  const proto = c.prototype
  proto.weekYear = function () {
    const month = this.month()
    const weekOfYear = this.week()
    const year = this.year()
    if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
      return year + 1
    }
    if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) {
      return year - 1
    }
    return year
  }
}
```

